assessments.evidence:
T10.1 builds 5 malformations × (6 permutations of ok/mismatch/bad + 2 of mismatch/bad) = 40 documents, each expecting exactly ScriptHashInputError.
Each malformation is malformed in isolation:
- +'00' gives total 176 against header 58ad;
- uppercase hash;
- non-empty parameters;
- parameters null;
- empty title.
Across the permutations the mismatch takes every position (0-2 in triples, 0-1 in pairs). The first-error-in-document-order mutant fails the 4 orders per malformation where the mismatch comes first.
T10.2 covers mismatch-only cases: nibble flip ×3 positions, code byte 100 (still admitted by C4) ×3 positions, and both pair orders, all exactly Mismatch. This kills first-only and last-only recompute shortcuts. Positive controls: base, plus the three-entry document giving {first, second, third: H}. Disclosed: message content and recompute-before-raise ordering are not observable.

Checker read in full (impl:1-203):
- imports hashlib and json only;
- seven constants, two sibling ValueError classes, ten functions;
- attribute set: issuperset, fromhex, blake2b().hexdigest, startswith, decode, json.loads, add, append;
- no I/O, environment, clock, random, subprocess, dunder, getattr, eval/exec or module-state write;
- messages carry only where-strings and validated hashes;
- library errors are mapped after their handlers exit.
Test loader (test:294-312): it reads at most 1 MiB+1 once, decodes strictly, and parses with ast.parse. The same allowlist and banned-name lint as the baseline (test:281-291) runs on that tree. It then execs compile(tree, …, dont_inherit=True) of the exact same linted AST object into a fresh types.ModuleType. There is no second read, SourceFileLoader, .pyc read or sys.path/sys.modules change. Traceback linecache reads are display-only.
It is lint, not a sandbox: exec inserts full builtins. The source-only residues are listed separately.

The proposal (CONTRACT:186-200, NOTES:110-137) matches the reviewed class:
- timeout 10s with kill-after 2s; prlimit cpu 10, as 536870912, fsize 2097152, core 0;
- bwrap --unshare-all --die-with-parent --new-session;
- ro /usr, /proc, minimal /dev;
- ro /input holding exactly the test; ro /packet holding exactly CIP-0057.md and SOURCES.json, the only files the test reads (_read is called with those two names only);
- modes 0444/0555 with no cache, symlink or extra entry;
- --clearenv with PATH, LANG and MHASH_PACKET_DIR;
- python3 -I -B /input/test_script_hash_addendum.py -v;
- before/after listings and pins, STOP on any difference, one attempt.
There are no writes, network, subprocess or out-of-scope imports. Native stdlib extensions (_hashlib, _blake2, _json) load as before. It correctly makes no read-only-root claim and discloses the tmpfs root and the -S/.pth residual.
The items A-F1 and A-F5 must be added when root freezes the exact argv: interpreter pin, capture bounding because fsize does not bound pipes, and treating start failures as STOP. These are freeze conditions, not source defects.

